  "prefLabel": "Puc 1106.03 Short Term Debt",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 1106.03 Short Term Debt. No utility shall issue or renew any notes, bonds or other evidences of indebtedness payable less than 12 months after the date thereof if said short term debt exceeds 10% of the utility's net fixed plant without prior commission approval pursuant to Puc 201.05.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter heading Puc 1100) #6445, eff 1-28-97; ss by #8244, eff 12-31-04; ss by #10307, eff 4-9-13",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc1100.html"
